      "title": "OpenAI introduces text watermarking in ChatGPT and Codex",
      "summary": "OpenAI is rolling out an invisible, machine-readable text watermarking feature called textGrain to ChatGPT and Codex, starting with users in the European Union to comply with EU AI Act requirements.",
      "design_implication": "When an editor reviews generated copy or a design system manager checks documentation provenance, machine-readable text markers become critical verification layers. Integrating visible inspection cues or metadata states directly into authoring tools helps teams track content origins without breaking editorial flow.",
